{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — Rabbi Moses said: <b>for He has remembered us (זכרנו)</b> — our males, and <b>He will bless the house of Israel</b> — the females. This is not correct, for the house of Aaron are not females. <b>A man and his house</b> throughout all of Scripture — only <b>זכרנו</b> is from the root of זכירה (remembrance), and the sign of this is that it has a kamatz gadol, for if it were from the root of זכרים (males), the resh would have a kamatz katan. Rather, the meaning is that HaShem has always remembered us. <b>He will bless</b> — those who trust in Him; and He returns to mention them again."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 115, :notes {0 "The comment as transmitted appears slightly disordered; the phrase 'רק הטעם' (rather, the meaning) seems to resume the main argument after the grammatical excursus. Rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:46.452190587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}